What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/ade0000.clock-controller/probe_phase
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        https://github.com/MCC45TR/senemos-uke-kernel-mainline
Description:
                Read-only final probe phase. Examples include proxy-votes,
                runtime-resume, critical-gate-write, critical-gate-read,
                critical-gate-verify, crm-admission, and ready. A quarantined
                failure preserves its first phase until reboot. Ready means
                provider registration completed, not that cameras or runtime
                handoff passed. Clean failures can retry before publication.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/ade0000.clock-controller/probe_error
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        https://github.com/MCC45TR/senemos-uke-kernel-mainline
Description:
                Read-only signed errno returned at the final probe phase,
                or zero for successful registration. Later runtime faults
                remain separate in controller_state. The kernel fault log
                also records existing cached power/rollback errors and votes.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/ade0000.clock-controller/probe_gate_register
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        https://github.com/MCC45TR/senemos-uke-kernel-mainline
Description:
                Read-only hexadecimal offset of the last critical transport
                gate attempted during probe. ENODATA means no gate was reached.
                This is a cached offset, not an arbitrary register interface.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/ade0000.clock-controller/probe_gate_readback
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        https://github.com/MCC45TR/senemos-uke-kernel-mainline
Description:
                Read-only hexadecimal value from the existing readback of the
                gate named by probe_gate_register. ENODATA means that gate's
                update or read failed, or no gate was reached. Zero is a valid
                readback and differs from an unavailable observation. The
                value is retained even when the underlying register changes.
                None of these attributes reads MMIO, acquires runtime power,
                accesses EEPROM, or moves an actuator.
